# Dev server terminals

Before starting a dev server, check whether one is already running. Do not open another terminal for it if one exists.

## Check first

1. Read the terminals folder. The first lines of each session file have cwd, the last command, and whether a command is still running.
2. If a dev server for this project is already running, use that URL. Do not start a second one.

## If you start one

Stop that process when you are done. Do not leave a dev server you started running in the background.

```text
❌ BAD
Run `pnpm dev` without looking at open terminals. Leave it running after you finish.

✅ GOOD
See an existing `pnpm dev` for this project. Use that URL.
If none is running, start one, then stop it after you finish.
```
